{"book":24,"chapter":46,"context":{"chapter":46,"title":"Egypt Falls at Carchemish","summary":"The oracles against the nations begin with Egypt, whose proud army rises like the Nile in flood only to fall by the Euphrates at Carchemish. A second oracle foresees Nebuchadnezzar invading Egypt, and the chapter closes with comfort for Jacob.","background":"The battle of Carchemish in 605 BC, on the upper Euphrates, was one of the decisive battles of the ancient world: Babylon's crown prince Nebuchadnezzar crushed the Egyptian army, ending Egypt's hold on Syria and Judah (2 Kings 24:7). A Babylonian chronicle also records it. The ancient Greek translation places chapters 46–51 in the middle of chapter 25, in a different order.","customs":[{"term":"Brigandines","verses":"46:4","note":"Coats of armor made of small metal scales fastened to cloth or leather."}],"watchFor":["Egypt rising 'like a flood' (vv. 7–8), the image of its own Nile.","A mocking nickname: Pharaoh 'is but a noise; he hath passed the time appointed' (v. 17).","Verses 27–28 repeat the comfort of 30:10-11."],"connections":["2 Chronicles 35:20","2 Kings 23:29","2 Kings 24:7","Jeremiah 30:10-11"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["אֲשֶׁר","'asher","H834","HTr","which"],["הָיָה","hayah","H1961","HVqp3ms","it came"],["דְבַר","devar-","H1697","HNcmsc","[the] word of"],["יְהוָה","yahweh","H3068","HNpt","Yahweh"],["אֶל","'el-","H413","HR","to"],["יִרְמְיָהוּ","yirmeyahu","H3414","HNpm","Jeremiah"],["הַנָּבִיא","hanavi'","H5030","HTd/Ncmsa","the prophet"],["עַל","'al-","H5921","HR","on"],["הַגּוֹיִם","hagoyim","H1471","HTd/Ncmpa","the nations"]],"x":[[24001010,24001010,4],[38002008,38002008,3]],"xn":2},"2":{"w":[["לְמִצְרַיִם","lemitzrayim","H4714","HR/Npl","of Egypt"],["עַל","'al-","H5921","HR","on"],["חֵיל","cheil","H2428","HNcmsc","[the] army of"],["פַּרְעֹה","par'oh","H6547","HNtmsa","Pharaoh"],["נְכוֹ","nekho","H5224","HNpm","Necho"],["מֶלֶךְ","melekh","H4428","HNcmsc","[the] king of"],["מִצְרַיִם","mitzrayim","H4714","HNp